 "coaching_points": [
  "Warm-up 2-3 min \u2014 light jog, hip openers, leg swings, easy toe-taps on the ball before any hard reps.",
  "HOW PRESSURE WORKS: partner alternates roles \u2014 after feeding, the server steps up to the worker's back as a live defender within 2-3m so the touch must escape real pressure. Swap server/worker every 6 feeds.",
  "SCAN FIRST: before the ball arrives the worker glances over the shoulder to locate the pressure, then chooses the gate AWAY from it.",
  "First touch is directional and firm \u2014 take it across the defender's momentum into space, then explode through the gate in 2 touches max.",
  "Cushion the ball with a relaxed foot, push it into the gap, not under your feet \u2014 reset your body between reps to stay balanced.",
  "Server VARIES height and pace of the feed each rep so the worker adjusts the receiving surface every time.",
  "TARGET: 7 of 10 receptions must exit forward through a gate within 2 touches to count.",
  "VOLUME: 10 feeds per set, 4 sets; jogging the ball back to the server is your rest.",
  "Progression \u2014 hit 8/10 clean \u2192 server closes tighter and feeds harder; struggling at 5/10 \u2192 widen the gates and give a half-second more before closing."
 ],
 "variations": [
  "Weak foot only \u2014 every first touch and exit with the weak foot.",
  "Called gate \u2014 server shouts a gate as the ball travels; worker must exit through THAT one (forces late scan).",
  "Half-volley \u2014 server tosses a bouncing feed; worker takes one direct touch through a gate."
 ],
